# pyro_sourcefromlayer

- Label: Pyro Source from Layer
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 2 to 4
- Parameters: 37 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/pyro_sourcefromlayer.html
- Summary (EN): Adds density to a Float VDB using an envelope shape defined by Mono layers, combined with the existing VDB values through a chosen method (Add, Copy, Maximum, Average, Blend, Pull). The page states the node is available since 22.0.
- Résumé (FR) : Pyro Source from Layer ajoute de la densité à un VDB à partir d'une enveloppe dessinée par des calques Mono, sans activer de voxels nouveaux.

- Inputs meaning: ["source: Float VDB to modify", "thickness: Mono layer setting the envelope thickness at each pixel", "height: Mono layer setting where the envelope centre line sits", "density: Mono layer setting the envelope density"]

- Key parameters: ["Method: how envelope values combine with current VDB values (Add, Copy, Maximum, Average, Blend, Pull)", "Border: overrides the border mode used when sampling the reference layers; Auto uses the input layer mode", "Shape: Acceleration and Deceleration (pull strength toward current values), Blend, Scale, Thickness (global scale for the thickness input), Scale by Timestep, Falloff", "Enable Noise: scales envelope values with noise; Noise Scale, Element Size, Element Scale, Noise Offset, Noise Pulse", "Enable Distortion: distorts the envelope shape with noise; Distort Scale, Element Size, Element Scale, Distort Offset, Distort Pulse"]

- Caveats: ["The node does not activate voxels, so sources outside already-active areas have no effect", "Requires DOP-level permissions; not in Houdini Core, only in Houdini FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education"]

